{
  "_readme": [
    "SOURCES.json — where the shipped race music CAME FROM, and how to rebuild it.",
    "",
    "WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The .mp3s beside it are ARTIFACTS, not masters: they are",
    "the incompetech downloads re-encoded to VBR (see `encode` below). The masters",
    "are ~164 MB of 256-320 kbps CBR and are deliberately NOT in the working tree —",
    "for an ACQUIRED asset the reproducible source is a URL plus a hash plus an",
    "encode recipe, which is this file, not the bytes. (Contrast the CUES, which are",
    "GENERATED: their source is scripts/bake-cues.mjs and the artifacts are baked",
    "from it. Same principle, different kind of source.)",
    "",
    "`npm run fetch:music` rebuilds every shipped file from scratch: download the",
    "master, check it against `sha256`, run `encode`, write it here. `--verify` does",
    "the download and hash check only.",
    "",
    "THE HASH IS ON THE MASTER, NEVER ON THE OUTPUT. LAME is deterministic for a",
    "given version and settings, but two LAME versions do not agree byte for byte,",
    "so a re-encode on another machine is not reproducible AS BYTES and must not be",
    "gated as if it were. What IS gated is that the input is the same file",
    "(`sha256`) and that the result still sits at the loudness the catalogue trims",
    "it to (`npm run check:music-loudness`).",
    "",
    "NO NUMBER HERE IS ALSO SOMEWHERE ELSE. Titles, durations and the LUFS trims are",
    "public/display/audio/musicCatalogue.js (and, ported, native/libttp-runtime/ttp/",
    "audio.cc); the biome pools and the attribution text are CREDITS.txt. This file",
    "joins to those on `file` and re-declares none of it — CLAUDE.md manifest rule."
  ],
  "license": {
    "holder": "Kevin MacLeod",
    "license": "CC-BY 4.0",
    "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/",
    "source": "https://incompetech.com/music/royalty-free/music.html",
    "note": "Attribution is REQUIRED. See CREDITS.txt; the render-ready data is shared/credits.js."
  },
  "encode": {
    "tool": "ffmpeg",
    "args": [
      "-vn",
      "-map",
      "0:a",
      "-c:a",
      "libmp3lame",
      "-q:a",
      "5"
    ],
    "recordedWith": "ffmpeg 8.1.2 / libmp3lame",
    "note": [
      "-q:a 5 is ~130 kbps VBR: 164 MB of catalogue becomes ~80 MB, which is most of",
      "the preview deploy image. Songs STREAM one at a time through an <audio>",
      "element, so this is a deploy/clone cost rather than a per-player one.",
      "-vn strips the embedded cover art four of the masters carry.",
      "NO FILTERS, EVER. The per-song gains in musicCatalogue.js and audio.cc are",
      "AUTHORED LITERALS frozen against tests/fixtures/audio-corpus.jsonl, so an",
      "-af loudnorm here would silently invalidate the whole trim table. A plain",
      "re-encode holds integrated loudness to within ~0.1 LU, which is why the",
      "trims survived this one unchanged.",
      "MP3 IS NOT A QUALITY CHOICE. Opus/AAC at 96k are smaller and better per bit",
      "(~55 MB), but audio.cc bakes the path INCLUDING the extension into its SONG",
      "table and audio-corpus.jsonl froze those strings. That corpus can never be",
      "re-recorded (its JS oracle is deleted), so changing the extension turns",
      "audio_check and record_audio red on all four legs. Moving off MP3 means",
      "making Song::file a stem and letting each shell append its own extension —",
      "an ABI and corpus change, and a separate decision."
    ]
  },
